WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.381 --> 00:00:14.989
The monster yelled from inside the cave.

2
00:00:16.370 --> 00:00:17.591
ate the Tang Monk!

3
00:00:17.911 --> 00:00:19.792
So you might as well leave!"

4
00:00:21.533 --> 00:00:22.654
"Oh no!"

5
00:00:23.134 --> 00:00:25.996
Bajie fell to his knees and cried.

6
00:00:28.706 --> 00:00:30.287
wiped tears from his eyes.

7
00:00:30.307 --> 00:00:32.208
"Poor Master."

8
00:00:33.789 --> 00:00:35.691
Wukong frowned at his companions.

9
00:00:36.591 --> 00:00:38.733
can't believe you two believe that monster."

10
00:00:40.014 --> 00:00:40.594
He sighed.

11
00:00:40.614 --> 00:00:42.415
"Wait here."

12
00:00:44.217 --> 00:00:47.339
The monkey turned into a moth and flew into the cave.

13
00:00:48.640 --> 00:00:51.782
He soon found the Tang Monk tied up in a dark room.

14
00:00:52.722 --> 00:00:54.784
Wukong turned back into himself.

15
00:00:56.044 --> 00:00:57.644
"Wukong!" cried the Tang Monk.

16
00:01:00.625 --> 00:01:02.146
The monkey untied the monk.

17
00:01:02.166 --> 00:01:05.327
"We must be quiet."

18
00:01:06.507 --> 00:01:08.067
Wukong recited a spell.

19
00:01:11.328 --> 00:01:15.149
A moment later the sound of snoring drifted into the room.

20
00:01:17.850 --> 00:01:20.631
spell put the monster and demons to sleep," said the monkey.

21
00:01:20.651 --> 00:01:26.808
"Let's go."

22
00:01:27.228 --> 00:01:29.090
and the monk came out of the cave.

23
00:01:30.110 --> 00:01:32.012
Bajie and Wujing were thrilled.

24
00:01:32.872 --> 00:01:36.294
"Master, we thought you'd been eaten," said Bajie.

25
00:01:36.315 --> 00:01:39.917
"I knew he was fine," said Wukong.

26
00:01:40.777 --> 00:01:43.699
"Now I'm going to make sure these villains never bother anyone again."

27
00:01:45.601 --> 00:01:47.462
He pulled out his iron bar.

28
00:01:50.304 --> 00:01:53.526
It grew until it was the size of a very tall tree.

29
00:01:53.546 --> 00:01:56.268
"Stand back," said the monkey.

30
00:02:01.324 --> 00:02:05.107
With one swing Wukong smashed the entire cave.

31
00:02:06.448 --> 00:02:09.430
Rocks exploded and fell on top of one another.

32
00:02:11.071 --> 00:02:13.593
Wukong looked at the rubble and smiled.

33
00:02:16.195 --> 00:02:19.538
Weeks went by, and the travelers arrived in a small town.

34
00:02:20.899 --> 00:02:23.060
Bajie's stomach growled loudly.

35
00:02:24.862 --> 00:02:29.180
laughed. "I guess we should look for food."

36
00:02:29.280 --> 00:02:31.782
They saw an old monk walking down a street.

37
00:02:34.004 --> 00:02:35.725
"Kind monk," said the Tang Monk.

38
00:02:36.585 --> 00:02:38.247
you know where we can beg for some food?

39
00:02:39.007 --> 00:02:39.888
We are quite hungry."

40
00:02:41.209 --> 00:02:42.309
old monk nodded.

41
00:02:42.950 --> 00:02:45.311
"Go to Squire Kou's house.

42
00:02:46.092 --> 00:02:50.055
The squire made a vow to feed ten thousand Buddhist monks.

43
00:02:51.196 --> 00:02:53.237
He will surely give you some food."

44
00:02:54.778 --> 00:02:57.100
He gave the Tang Monk directions to the house.

45
00:02:58.252 --> 00:02:59.733
"Thank you," said the Tang Monk.

46
00:03:01.795 --> 00:03:05.357
The travelers arrived at the squire's gate, and a servant let them in.

47
00:03:07.699 --> 00:03:10.541
The squire's house was very large and fancy.

48
00:03:12.022 --> 00:03:13.683
Squire Kou came outside.

49
00:03:15.704 --> 00:03:16.845
he said with a smile.

50
00:03:16.865 --> 00:03:19.027
"Please come inside."

51
00:03:20.448 --> 00:03:23.210
The travelers sat with the squire in a large room.

52
00:03:24.370 --> 00:03:26.212
A servant brought tea and snacks.

53
00:03:27.608 --> 00:03:30.290
"Thank you for inviting us in, Squire," said the Tang Monk.

54
00:03:30.310 --> 00:03:33.951
"We heard that you made a vow to feed ten thousand monks."

55
00:03:35.873 --> 00:03:36.613
said the squire.

56
00:03:36.633 --> 00:03:39.474
"I've made plenty of money during my life.

57
00:03:40.395 --> 00:03:42.456
But I want to do good deeds as well.

58
00:03:43.457 --> 00:03:47.319
I hope to be reborn one day as a bodhisattva or even a buddha."

59
00:03:48.659 --> 00:03:52.662
"Well, Squire," said Bajie, "today's your lucky day!

60
00:03:52.682 --> 00:03:56.824
I can easily eat as much food as ten thousand monks.

61
00:03:58.312 --> 00:04:01.433
if you feed me, you'll definitely become a buddha!"

62
00:04:02.474 --> 00:04:04.855
Everybody laughed.

63
00:04:04.995 --> 00:04:07.996
"It my lucky day," said the squire.

64
00:04:08.016 --> 00:04:12.038
"Last night I checked to see how many monks I've fed.

65
00:04:13.238 --> 00:04:17.400
So far I've fed 9,996 monks.

66
00:04:18.480 --> 00:04:21.762
I need to feed only four more in order to fulfill my vow."

67
00:04:22.842 --> 00:04:24.703
smile spread across his face.

68
00:04:24.723 --> 00:04:29.369
"And there are four of you!"

69
00:04:29.629 --> 00:04:32.011
evening Squire Kou held a feast.

70
00:04:33.192 --> 00:04:34.834
Everybody in the town was invited.

71
00:04:36.035 --> 00:04:39.398
The travelers sat with the squire and his wife, Lady Kou.

72
00:04:40.559 --> 00:04:44.842
Bajie drooled as he gazed at all of the wonderful food on the table.

73
00:04:44.862 --> 00:04:51.708
"Noodles, buns, mushrooms I don't know what to eat first!"

74
00:04:55.131 --> 00:04:58.637
As they ate, Squire Kou leaned toward the Tang Monk.

75
00:04:58.657 --> 00:05:02.158
"So where are you and your companions going?"

76
00:05:03.499 --> 00:05:06.120
"We're traveling to the Western Paradise," said the monk.

77
00:05:06.140 --> 00:05:09.561
"We're going to fetch the True Scriptures from Buddha."

78
00:05:10.782 --> 00:05:12.242
The squire's eyes lit up.

79
00:05:13.823 --> 00:05:15.043
are special guests!

80
00:05:16.063 --> 00:05:16.684
I can't let you
